          "english_quote": "Allow me to know these matters better than you do.",
          "issue": "In modern English, “Allow me to know” reads as a request for permission rather than a demand to concede Appion’s existing superior knowledge. The lexical note correctly identifies the concessive sense of συγχώρει, but the main wording does not clearly express it.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use “Grant that I know these matters better than you do” or “Concede that I know more about these matters than you do.”",
